<p>This was worth the wait my man, thanks.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">So&nbsp;are&nbsp;you&nbsp;from&nbsp;Sesame&nbsp;Street...</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Or&nbsp;more&nbsp;Kermit&nbsp;the&nbsp;frog?</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>Not everything needs a backstory</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I just didn't want to say &quot;It just happened one day.&quot; y'know?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>lack of connection to Chicago Spirit</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Down one of these crit chains I came up with this: They are a poor immigrant with their family, and have to join CS at age 16 to make ends meet. They choose the spirit because Para-Crime pays more than the competitors. They start as a pickpocket, but after the spirit realize they made him anomalous, he get promoted to &quot;Heist Plan-B&quot;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The description here took me a second to understand what was going on.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I was trying to be concise, so here is a description of the blood creature</p>
<blockquote>
<p>A humanoid made entirely of SCP-XXX's blood. It stands at a height of 180 centimeter, same as SCP-XXX. The blood appears to be flowing. To date, it has never successfully been terminated other than by completing SCP-XXX's escape.</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>this feels somewhat farfetched due to the (supposed) criminal background this person has.</p>
