<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre (Optional):</strong> Emotional</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout:</strong> The page will begin with a simple description of the SCP and after that, the investigation of containing it.</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> We can see the researcher ask for a member of Gamer Against Weed to help him to contain SCP-XXXX.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> Ok, so basically, the SCP is a drug that makes all the people that sniff it is all good and all of that. The anomaly is that it can't be stopped and will have some kind of dependence over it even when all the traces of it are being wiped out. So there's a containment breach over the site that contains it and the foundation try all they can to contain SCP-XXXX. A scientist has this idea about cooperating with Gamer Against Weed because of their experience with the drug SCP. Of course, the chance of GAW having actually experience with the drugs SCP is really little but it's their only chance. So the researcher that has found the idea will communicate with GAW and try to cooperate with them.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> The originality of my idea is that we never actually get to have Gamer Against Weed to be more serious and actually be not the kind of Goi that is just here for the laughs. Of course, they will still be the classic version.</p>

